; Example 3: encode then decode round-trip
; ENC processes cnt vectors, writes packed bytes to HBM at [dst].
; DEC reads the EncodeResult state and reconstructs Cartesian vectors.
; Combined: input[0..cnt-1] -> compressed -> reconstructed at [dst+offset].
; Useful for validation: measure RMSE between input and decoded.

; Save original vector info (emulator stores result internally)
ENC [0x00000000], [0x10000000], 1

; DEC reconstructs from the internal EncodeResult
DEC [0x10000000], [0x20000000], 1
HALT
